# Header rules for static hosts that read this file (Cloudflare Pages,
# Netlify). Served from the site root.
#
# There is no .wasm and no .mjs here any more -- the app is plain .js ES
# modules -- so the MIME pins that B9 forced are no longer load-bearing. What
# remains is worth keeping on its own terms: nosniff, so a host that guesses
# a type cannot turn one of these files into something else, and a referrer
# policy, because a build script's filename has no business leaking.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
